<title>USA: ConAgra confirms talks to buy stake in Indian firm.</title>
<headline>ConAgra confirms talks to buy stake in Indian firm.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>ConAgra Inc, a diversified food company, confirmed Tuesday it is in talks to acquire a majority stake in ITC Agro-Tech Ltd, an Indian agribusiness company.</p>
<p>But no agreement has been reached to take a stake in the company, 41 percent of which is now held by ITC Ltd.</p>
<p>&quot;We have not signed anything,&quot; a ConAgra spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>She gave no details about the negotiations, but said talks were in line with what was described in a newspaper report.</p>
<p>The Business Standard newspaper of Bombay reported that ConAgra was in talks to acquire 51.29 percent of ITC Agro-Tech.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
